## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CV design with 3D reconstruction, uncertainty, and fast on-device adaptation, crucial for tool manipulation in cluttered spaces.

## Key Concepts
- 3D pose + mesh prediction from monocular input
- Uncertainty estimation and active adaptation
- Edge-efficient architectures and losses for consistency

## Code Example
```javascript
function loss(params){
  const L2 = reprojLoss(params);
  const Lpose = poseLoss(params);
  const Lmesh = meshLoss(params);
  const Lreg = temporalEdgeReg(params);
  return L2 + Lpose + Lmesh + Lreg;
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you calibrate uncertainty for active-learning? 
- What would you change for multiple simultaneous tools?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design joint monocular depth and motion estimation under dynamic scenes and adverse weather, optimized for edge devices and quick adaptation to new conditions.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular depth and scene-flow fusion in cluttered traffic
- Temporal fusion across frames for stability
- On-device 5-shot adaptation with lightweight adapters

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-architecture sketch
function forward(x) {
  const z = encoder(x); // shared features
  const d = depthHead(z);
  const s = flowHead(z);
  const o = objMotionHead(z);
  const t = temporalFuse([d, s, o]);
  return {depth: d, sceneFlow: s, objectMotion: o, fused: t};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure edge-device latency vs. accuracy across weather scenarios?
- Which datasets and metrics would you prioritize for evaluation and validation?

## Why This Is Asked
This assesses end-to-end CV system design on monocular input, 3D reconstruction, semantic/kinematic outputs, and on-device adaptation, under real-world constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular depth/3D reconstruction
- Voxel-based 3D representation and BEV outputs
- Multi-task objectives: occupancy, semantics, motion tracking
- Self-supervision with ego-motion and photometric consistency
- Lightweight 3-shot on-device adaptation via adapters

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation sketch
async function runPipeline(frame) {
  const latent = encode(frame)
  const voxels = decodeToVoxels(latent)
  return { occupancy: voxelToOccupancy(voxels), beings: trackPedestrians(latent) }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate 3D occupancy accuracy vs. GT? 
- How would you extend to multi-camera fusion or hinge on motion blur?
